# .gitignore
# This file tells Git which files/folders to IGNORE - meaning they will
# never be uploaded to GitHub, even though they exist in your project folder.

# --- The database file ---
# This is the most important line in this file. land_farmer.db will contain
# real customer names, phone numbers, emails, and ID numbers once you start
# using the app for real. Database files should never be uploaded to GitHub,
# even in a private repository - it's just good practice to keep real data
# out of version control entirely. Anyone who downloads this project will
# just run database_setup.py themselves to create their own empty database.
land_farmer.db

# --- Python's own generated files ---
# Every time you run a Python file, Python creates a "__pycache__" folder
# full of pre-compiled files to make the next run slightly faster. These
# are automatically regenerated and never need to be uploaded.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# --- Virtual environment folders ---
# If you ever create a virtual environment (a "uv venv" or "venv" folder)
# inside this project folder, it should never be uploaded either - it can
# be several hundred megabytes, and anyone can recreate it instantly from
# requirements.txt instead.
.venv/
venv/

# --- Operating system files ---
# Windows and Mac automatically create small hidden files in every folder
# you browse. These have nothing to do with your project.
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
